BUG: `DateTime.fromISO("1974-01-06", { zone: "America/Los_Angeles" }).isInDST` returns false, but US DST began 1974-01-06, so it must be true. Root cause: the `isInDST` getter probes the offset in January of the same year via `this.set({ month: 1 })`, which keeps the day-of-month; for 1974 the January probe therefore lands on/after the Jan 6 transition and is itself in DST, so the comparison fails. (Confirmed empirically: the environment's tz data is correct - LA 1974 spring-forward is 1974-01-06 02:00 PST -> 03:00 PDT.)

APPLY THIS EXACT CHANGE to the `get isInDST()` getter in /luxon/src/datetime.js (it currently reads `this.offset > this.set({ month: 1 }).offset || this.offset > this.set({ month: 5 }).offset`):

  get isInDST() {
    if (this.isOffsetFixed) {
      return false;
    } else {
      return (
        this.offset > this.set({ month: 1, day: 1 }).offset ||
        this.offset > this.set({ month: 5 }).offset
      );
    }
  }

(i.e. only add `day: 1` to the January probe, keeping the JSDoc comment and prettier formatting intact).

